Currently `main()` does two fetches. After migration, there is one fetch. The `extractRateLimitGroups()` function (lines 343-366) already works with the OpenAPI operation structure; it just needs to receive operations from the same spec object. Since the unified `OpenApiOperation` interface now includes both `x-cache-age` and `x-rate-limit`, all extraction functions can operate on the same spec.

Remove the second fetch block entirely (lines 534-546). Change the `extractRateLimitGroups()` call to pass the same `spec` object. The function's `OpenApiSpec` type is now the same unified type.

