#### Step 1.3: Build a `$ref` Resolver

The OpenAPI spec uses `$ref` in two places:
1. Response schemas: `responses.200.content['application/json'].schema.$ref` pointing to `#/components/schemas/AllianceDetail`
2. Properties within schemas: e.g., `creator_corporation_id: { $ref: "#/components/schemas/CorporationID" }` -- these 9 common ID types (`AllianceID`, `CharacterID`, `CorporationID`, `FactionID`, etc.) all resolve to `{ type: "integer", format: "int64" }`

The resolver function:

```typescript
function resolveRef(spec: OpenApiSpec, ref: string): OpenApiSchema | undefined {
  // Handles "#/components/schemas/Foo"
  const prefix = '#/components/schemas/';
  if (!ref.startsWith(prefix)) return undefined;
  const schemaName = ref.slice(prefix.length);
  return spec.components?.schemas?.[schemaName];
}

function resolveSchema(spec: OpenApiSpec, schema: OpenApiSchema): OpenApiSchema {
  if (schema.$ref) {
    const resolved = resolveRef(spec, schema.$ref);
    if (resolved) return resolveSchema(spec, resolved); // recursive for chained refs
  }
  return schema;
}
```

This must be called:
- When extracting the response schema for an endpoint
- When processing each property within a schema (to resolve ID type refs)
- When processing `items` of array schemas

