### Risks and Mitigations

| Risk | Severity | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| `x-cache-age` unit differs from `x-cached-seconds` | High | Check actual values in OpenAPI spec before trusting the assumption. If values are in different units, add a conversion. The contract test for cache TTL drift will catch mismatches. |
| `$ref` chains -- a `$ref` pointing to another `$ref` | Medium | The `resolveSchema` function uses recursion. The 9 known common ID types are terminal (no further refs), but defensive recursion handles any future chains. |
| Some OpenAPI response schemas may be inline (not `$ref`) | Medium | The `generateInterface` function must handle both `$ref` and inline schemas. The fallback path from the current code is preserved. |
| OpenAPI spec may have additional endpoints not in Swagger | Low | This is a feature. The 182 vs 180 path count difference means 2 additional endpoints get types. |
| `EsiSpec` namespace types change names -- consumers break | Medium | This is expected for a major version. The types are documented as generated/internal. The `EsiOperationTypes` mapping at the bottom of the generated file will also have updated type names. |
| The `EsiOperationTypes` interface maps `operationId` to response types | Medium | The `operationId` values are the same between Swagger and OpenAPI specs. Only the type names change. Verify that `operationId` values match. |

